      "y": -470,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "13 PROGRAM PAGES \u2014 every word is the client's own, verbatim from their live site.\n\nTHIS ROUND:\n\u00b7 Type scale raised throughout \u2014 headings and body copy were too small to read at 100%.\n\u00b7 The gold washes and the Request Information band now BOUNCE, sweeping corner to corner on a rAF loop (never a CSS animation, which your browser pauses).\n\u00b7 Request Information band is the sand gradient, mapped onto your golds.\n\u00b7 OPEN GYM is the framed-hero test: photo inset in a rounded panel with black around it, title centred. Approve and it rolls to the other 12.\n\u00b7 Open Gym also drops the cage/mats copy and moves to fitness-floor and turf photos.\n\nCLASS TIMES ARE SHARED \u2014 no page has a schedule typed into it; all read data/classes.json. Adult pages exclude kids classes; kids pages carry their own.\n\nStill coming: header dropdown, mobile artboards, then coaches, FAQ, Events and Sponsors."
    },
    {
      "id": "sched-note",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 680,
      "text": "MASTER SCHEDULE \u2014 all 86 classes, times aligned across the week. Filter chips work: Adults (69), Kids (12), Fitness (5).\n\nThis grid and every program page read the same file, so a class edited once moves everywhere."
